# =========================================================================
# DEPENDENCY OVERRIDES EXPLANATION
# =========================================================================
# We are forcing 'js-yaml' to '^5.2.2' via package.json overrides.
# This patches a High-Severity Denial of Service vulnerability (CVE-2026-73643).
# It fixes the nested dependency inside @nestjs/swagger without triggering
# the breaking changes associated with a full '@nestjs/swagger' upgrade.
# =========================================================================

# =========================================================================
# TYPESCRIPT ARCHITECTURE & COMPILER CONFIGURATION NOTES
# =========================================================================
# 
# 1. DEPRECATION & REMOVAL OF "baseUrl":
#    We are explicitly commenting out the "baseUrl" property. In the 
#    TypeScript compiler engine, "baseUrl" was formally deprecated and 
#    completely dropped as of TypeScript 7.0. All modern path mappings 
#    now directly rely on explicit absolute-relative values mapped under 
#    the "paths" property to prevent layout errors.
#
# 2. ISOLATED GLOBAL TYPINGS VIA THE "types" MATRIX:
#    We are intentionally retaining the explicit ["node", "jest"] array values. 
#    Relying on TypeScript's default autodiscover environment sweeps inside 
#    "node_modules/@types" forces the engine to greedily compile hundreds of 
#    unrelated, transitive global type definitions into the namespace. 
#    Hardcoding this matrix isolates scope and prevents toxic type leaks.
#
# =========================================================================